description: Require manual user verification before any git action
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git Actions Require Manual Verification

Any action that uses git (commit, push, pull, branch rename/delete, remote
changes, `gh` commands affecting the repo, etc.) must be explicitly confirmed
by the user before execution, even if it seems routine or was implied by an
earlier instruction.

- Before running the command, state exactly what git action you intend to
  take and why.
- Wait for explicit user confirmation ("yes", "go ahead", etc.) before
  running it.
- This applies regardless of whether the command would normally be
  auto-approved.
